{
  "id": "ui-testimonial-row",
  "title": "Testimonial row: three quote cards from one component over a Static Data array",
  "description": "Three quotes, one card component, no hand-written copies — the same rule as the stat tile row and the footer, and the reason it matters here is that three testimonials are the most tempting place to paste a subtree three times. Each card is a real designed object rather than a paragraph in a column: a --surface fill, a hairline border, a radius, and a soft shadow so it sits ABOVE the band rather than in it. Two details do most of the work. The quote glyph is set in --border, not --muted-foreground, so it reads as ornament rather than as a word. The author row is an Image and two lines of text with a columnGap and alignItems center — a portrait pressed against its own name is the single commonest spacing tell in generated pages, and a gap is what fixes it. Wire `items` from Query Records to make it live; the Static Data node is the shape of the row, and it is worth keeping as the empty-state seed.",
  "demonstrates": [
    "Static Data",
    "For Each",
    "net.noodl.visual.columns",
    "Group",
    "Image",
    "Text",
    "Component Inputs"
  ],
